<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Triple inverted pendulum · Control Lab</title><style>[hidden]{display:none!important}#lqr{touch-action:none;cursor:grab}#lqr:active{cursor:grabbing}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf2f5;color:#173443;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1200px;margin:24px auto;padding:34px;background:white;border-radius:24px}a{color:#087e82}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);letter-spacing:-1.6px;line-height:1.1;margin:16px 0}h2{font-size:19px;margin:0}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#008780}.intro{max-width:730px;color:#617782}.controls{display:flex;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;padding:18px;background:#edf5f5;border-radius:14px;margin:25px 0}label{display:grid;gap:5px;font-size:12px}button,select{padding:11px 16px;border:1px solid #c8d9dd;border-radius:9px;background:white;color:#173443;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}button.primary{background:#173443;color:white}.time{flex:1;min-width:180px}input{width:100%;accent-color:#07867e}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.panel{border:1px solid #e1e9ed;border-radius:15px;padding:18px;min-width:0;background:#f9fbfc}.panel canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:560px}.panel{background:#f6f9fb;overflow:hidden}.status{min-height:40px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.time span{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.status{font-size:12px;min-height:20px;margin:6px 0;color:#637b85}.plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin:22px 0}.plots canvas{width:100%;height:215px;display:block}figure{margin:0;min-width:0}figcaption{font-weight:600}.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;font-size:12px;margin:18px 0}.legend i{display:inline-block;width:20px;border-top:3px solid;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7eb}.note{font-size:12px;color:#607782}details{padding:15px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7eb}summary{font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}code{background:#edf3f6;padding:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}footer{margin-top:22px;font-size:12px;color:#607782}@media(max-width:800px){.plots{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:18px;margin:6px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style></head><body><main>
<a href="index.html">Single pendulum</a> · <a href="double.html">Double pendulum</a>
<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:24px">CONTROL LAB / THREE LINKS, ONE ACTUATOR</div><h1>Three pendulums. One force.</h1>
<p class="intro">Eight state variables, three coupled angles, and one horizontal actuator. Explore a nonlinear triple-pendulum simulation with the same 8 N force limit and ±2 m travel cutoff.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Experiment<select id="case"><option id="swing-option" value="swingup" selected>Start hanging down · swing up and balance</option><option value="aligned">Aligned lean · +1° / +1° / +1°</option><option value="opposed">Opposing lean · +1° / −1° / +1°</option><option value="push">External push · 3 N for 0.2 s</option></select></label><label>Playback speed<select id="speed"><option value="0.25">0.25× · inspect</option><option value="0.5">0.5× · slow motion</option><option value="1" selected>1× · real time</option><option value="2">2× · faster viewing</option></select></label><button class="primary" id="play">Play</button><button id="reset">Restart</button><label class="time">Time <span id="time-label">0.00 s</span><input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="12" step=".02" value="0" aria-label="Time in seconds"></label></div>
<p id="interaction-note" class="note">Grab any coloured joint. The dashed tether applies a physical force; all three free hinges and rigid links respond together. Only the cart is motorised. After release, recovery may first settle the links downward, then raise them again. This can take tens of seconds; watch the phase label.</p><p id="planning-note" class="note"></p><p id="explanation"></p>
<div class="pair"><section class="panel"><h2 id="control-title">Planned swing-up + LQR</h2><p id="lqr-status" class="status"></p><canvas id="lqr" role="img" aria-label="Controlled triple pendulum"></canvas></section></div>
<p class="note">Absolute angles from upward vertical. Cart travel and link lengths use the same metre scale, fixed throughout each experiment. The coloured links rotate in front of the rear guide rail; contact is not modelled. Three fading trails show the last second of motion of each coloured point; the red arrow indicates actuator force. Playback speed changes viewing time only. Near-upright trials stop at 60° tilt; swing-up permits full rotations. All trials stop at ±2 m cart travel. These cutoffs do not model collisions.</p>
<div class="legend"><span><i style="color:#15938b"></i>Lower link θ₁</span><span><i style="color:#7964b8"></i>Middle link θ₂</span><span><i style="color:#d78b32"></i>Upper link θ₃</span></div>
<div class="plots" id="recorded-plots"><figure><figcaption>Three angles to balance</figcaption><canvas id="angles" role="img" aria-label="Three angles versus time"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Cart position · controlled</figcaption><canvas id="position" role="img" aria-label="Cart position in metres"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Actuator force · controlled</figcaption><canvas id="force" role="img" aria-label="Actuator force in newtons"></canvas></figure></div>
<div id="recorded-results"><h2>Controlled-run results</h2><div style="overflow:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Settling time</th><th>Peak force</th><th>Squared-force effort</th></tr></thead><tbody id="metrics"></tbody></table></div>
<p class="note">Settling requires cart error ≤ 2 cm, speed ≤ 0.03 m/s, all angles ≤ 1° and all angular speeds ≤ 0.05 rad/s for the remainder of the run, with at least 1 s remaining. Time is measured from simulation start, after the push ends or after the swing-up handoff. Effort is ∫u²dt, not energy. A stopped trial has a shorter evaluation horizon.</p>
</div><details><summary>How the controller works</summary><p>Near upright, an eight-state LQR uses cart position/velocity and all three angles/angular velocities. Its gain is calculated for this model; it is not copied from the two-link controller.</p><p id="gain"></p><p>The hanging-start trial tracks an offline nonlinear reference with time-varying LQR for six seconds, then switches to upright LQR. The shown trajectory is independently integrated from the nonlinear equations with actuator saturation. This demonstrates one nominal manoeuvre, not global recovery from arbitrary states.</p></details>
<details><summary>Model and limitations</summary><p>Dragging continues the same eight-state nonlinear model. Three massless rigid links are connected by free, frictionless hinges, with a point mass at each endpoint. The cart alone is motorised (±8 N). A virtual mouse spring (3 N/m, damping 0.025 N·s/m, force magnitude capped at 0.12 N) applies force to the selected point through its position Jacobian. No joint motor, angle target or inverse-kinematic correction is applied. During swing-up the original time-varying cart controller continues; afterwards the upright LQR acts. Strong disturbances can cause a fall. Outside the local tracking envelope, the upright/tracking law is smoothly reduced and a cart-only braking law takes over (up to 2 N); no joint is driven. Angles are compared modulo a full turn. After a fall, a cart-only controller stabilises the hanging equilibrium, then restarts the six-second swing-up reference only once position, angle and velocity tolerances have been met for 0.25 seconds. No rod or mass is repositioned. This is a tested recovery strategy, not a global stability guarantee. The mouse tether engages over 0.08 s and its target is filtered over 0.05 s to avoid abrupt cursor inputs. Live integration stops at ±2 m cart travel; impacts and link contact are not modelled.</p><p>Cart: 0.8 kg. Three point masses: 0.2/3 kg each. Three massless rods: 0.5/3 m each. Gravity: 9.81 m/s². Cart friction: 0.08 N·s/m. The single, double and triple examples share total suspended mass and upright height, but not mass distribution.</p><p>Q = diag(10,1,100,1,100,1,100,1), R = 0.1 in the documented SI state units. Ideal full-state sensing, no noise, actuator delay or joint friction. Local LQR optimality does not extend automatically to the nonlinear, saturated system.</p><p>RK4 step: 0.0025 s. Playback samples: 0.02 s, interpolated using positions and velocities. Rod lengths stay fixed; recorded forces and numerical results are unchanged. Initial lean is 1° here versus 3° in the double example, so their recovery times are not a matched benchmark. The external push experiment compares saved single-, double- and triple-link runs with the same 3 N pulse, total mass, height, time step and force limit. The state dimensions, mass distributions and LQR objectives differ. Increasing link count does not alone establish a universal performance ranking.</p></details>
<footer>English educational simulation · <a href="../README.md">Model, reproducibility and research notes</a>.</footer></main>
<script id="data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id);let c,t=0,playing=false,last=0,raf=0,scene=null,lastPlot=-1,interactive=null,drag=null,dragId=null,view=null,liveTrail=[],accumulator=0,physicalStop=false,recovery=null;const teal='#15938b',purple='#7964b8';
function sample(rows,time){if(time<=rows[0][0])return rows[0];if(time>=rows.at(-1)[0])return rows.at(-1);let i=Math.min(rows.length-2,Math.max(0,Math.floor(time/.02)));while(i>0&&rows[i][0]>time)i--;while(i<rows.length-2&&rows[i+1][0]<time)i++;const a=rows[i],b=rows[i+1],h=b[0]-a[0],f=(time-a[0])/h,out=a.map((v,k)=>v+f*(b[k]-v));if(a.length>=11)for(const k of [1,3,5,7]){out[k]=(2*f**3-3*f*f+1)*a[k]+(f**3-2*f*f+f)*h*a[k+1]+(-2*f**3+3*f*f)*b[k]+(f**3-f*f)*h*b[k+1];out[k+1]=((6*f*f-6*f)*a[k]+(-6*f*f+6*f)*b[k])/h+(3*f*f-4*f+1)*a[k+1]+(3*f*f-2*f)*b[k+1]}return out}
function joints(row){const points=[[row[1],0]];for(const k of [3,5,7]){const a=points.at(-1);points.push([a[0]+Math.sin(row[k])/6,a[1]+Math.cos(row[k])/6])}return points}
function sceneBounds(){let xmin=-.35,xmax=.35,ymin=-.5,ymax=.5;for(const key of ['lqr'])for(const row of c[key].data)for(const [x,y] of joints(row)){xmin=Math.min(xmin,x);xmax=Math.max(xmax,x);ymin=Math.min(ymin,y);ymax=Math.max(ymax,y)}return{xmin:xmin-.13,xmax:xmax+.13,ymin:ymin-.09,ymax:ymax+.09}}

function canvas(id,h){const el=$(id),w=el.clientWidth,d=window.devicePixelRatio||1;if(el.width!==Math.round(w*d)||el.height!==Math.round(h*d)){el.width=Math.round(w*d);el.height=Math.round(h*d)}const ctx=el.getContext('2d');ctx.setTransform(d,0,0,d,0,0);ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);return[ctx,w,h]}
function rig(key){const [ctx,w]=canvas(key,560),row=interactive?[t,...interactive,recovery.force(interactive),0]:sample(c[key].data,t),m=interactive?{end_s:Infinity,status:"completed"}:c[key].metrics,scale=Math.min((w-36)/(scene.xmax-scene.xmin),470/(scene.ymax-scene.ymin)),X=x=>w/2+(x-(scene.xmin+scene.xmax)/2)*scale,Y=y=>275-(y-(scene.ymin+scene.ymax)/2)*scale,x=X(row[1]),y=Y(0);view={scale,ox:X(0),oy:Y(0)};ctx.lineCap='round';ctx.lineJoin='round';
// Grid and rear guide rail use the same length scale as every link.
ctx.strokeStyle='#e5edf2';ctx.lineWidth=1;for(let gx=Math.ceil(scene.xmin/.25)*.25;gx<=scene.xmax;gx+=.25){ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(gx),32);ctx.lineTo(X(gx),515);ctx.stroke()}ctx.setLineDash([3,6]);ctx.strokeStyle='#c3d3dd';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(0),30);ctx.lineTo(X(0),515);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.strokeStyle='#bbcbd5';ctx.lineWidth=7;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(14,y+16);ctx.lineTo(w-14,y+16);ctx.stroke();ctx.strokeStyle='#edf3f7';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(14,y+14);ctx.lineTo(w-14,y+14);ctx.stroke();
// Three fading trails, each attached to its own point mass.
const end=Math.min(t,m.end_s),trailColours=[teal,purple,'#d78b32'],trail=[];for(let j=0;j<=50;j++)trail.push(joints(sample(interactive?liveTrail:c[key].data,Math.max(0,end-1+j*.02))));for(let point=1;point<=3;point++){ctx.strokeStyle=trailColours[point-1];ctx.lineWidth=2.2;for(let j=1;j<trail.length;j++){ctx.globalAlpha=.06+.64*j/(trail.length-1);ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(trail[j-1][point][0]),Y(trail[j-1][point][1]));ctx.lineTo(X(trail[j][point][0]),Y(trail[j][point][1]));ctx.stroke()}}ctx.globalAlpha=1;
// Carriage and bearing sit behind the rotating links (separate drawing planes).
ctx.fillStyle='#9eb2bf';ctx.fillRect(x-25,y+5,50,17);ctx.fillStyle='#223e50';ctx.beginPath();ctx.roundRect(x-30,y-13,60,29,7);ctx.fill();ctx.fillStyle='#426074';ctx.beginPath();ctx.roundRect(x-25,y-10,50,7,3);ctx.fill();for(const dx of [-20,20]){ctx.fillStyle='#c6d3db';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x+dx,y+17,5,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill();ctx.fillStyle='#526b7a';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x+dx,y+17,2,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill()}
const pts=joints(row),colours=[teal,purple,'#d78b32'];for(let i=0;i<3;i++){const a=pts[i],b=pts[i+1];ctx.strokeStyle='#385163';ctx.lineWidth=8;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(a[0]),Y(a[1]));ctx.lineTo(X(b[0]),Y(b[1]));ctx.stroke();ctx.strokeStyle=colours[i];ctx.lineWidth=4.5;ctx.stroke();ctx.strokeStyle='#ffffff88';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(a[0])-1,Y(a[1]));ctx.lineTo(X(b[0])-1,Y(b[1]));ctx.stroke()}for(let i=0;i<4;i++){const a=pts[i];ctx.fillStyle='#213c4d';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(X(a[0]),Y(a[1]),i?9:8,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill();ctx.fillStyle=i?colours[i-1]:'#d7e3e9';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(X(a[0]),Y(a[1]),i?6.5:5,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill();ctx.fillStyle='#f6fafc';ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(X(a[0]),Y(a[1]),2,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill()}
// Signed actuator force arrow; length is a display indicator, not distance.
if(Math.abs(row[9])>.1){const direction=Math.sign(row[9]),ax=x+direction*38,ay=y-25,bx=ax+direction*(8+Math.abs(row[9])*5);ctx.strokeStyle='#d05f50';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(ax,ay);ctx.lineTo(bx,ay);ctx.lineTo(bx-direction*6,ay-4);ctx.moveTo(bx,ay);ctx.lineTo(bx-direction*6,ay+4);ctx.stroke()}
ctx.fillStyle='#5b7280';ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.textAlign='left';ctx.fillText('FRONT VIEW · metres',16,20);ctx.strokeStyle='#607c8d';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(18,524);ctx.lineTo(18+.1*scale,524);ctx.stroke();ctx.fillText('0.10 m',18,539);ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText([3,5,7].map((col,i)=>`θ${i+1} ${((interactive?Math.atan2(Math.sin(row[col]),Math.cos(row[col])):row[col])*180/Math.PI).toFixed(1)}°`).join('   '),w-14,553);$(key+'-status').textContent=t>=m.end_s&&m.status!=='completed'?`Stabilisation failed at ${m.end_s.toFixed(3)} s · ${m.status==='tilt_limit'?'angle limit reached':'travel limit reached'} · Recorded trial ended`:`x ${row[1].toFixed(2)} m · force ${row[9].toFixed(2)} N${$('case').value==='swingup'?(key==='open'?' · hanging freely':t<6?' · tracking swing-up':' · upright LQR'):($('case').value==='push'&&t>=4&&t<4.2?' · external +3 N':'')}`;if(interactive){$(key+'-status').textContent=physicalStop?'Stopped: 2 m travel limit or numerical failure · Restart to repeat':(drag?'Dragging · physical tether · free hinges':recovery.label());if(drag){ctx.strokeStyle='#547384';ctx.lineWidth=1.5;ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);const end=joints(row)[drag.point];ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(end[0]),Y(end[1]));ctx.lineTo(X(drag.x),Y(drag.y));ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([])}}}

function plot(id,series,unit){const [ctx,w]=canvas(id,215),l=53,r=w-12,top=16,bottom=173;const vals=series.flatMap(s=>c[s.key].data.map(row=>row[s.col]*s.factor));vals.push(0);let low=Math.min(...vals),high=Math.max(...vals),pad=Math.max(.1,(high-low)*.1);low-=pad;high+=pad;const X=v=>l+v/12*(r-l),Y=v=>bottom-(v-low)/(high-low)*(bottom-top);ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.fillStyle='#617782';ctx.strokeStyle='#dce7eb';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.strokeRect(l,top,r-l,bottom-top);for(let i=0;i<=4;i++){let v=low+(high-low)*i/4;ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(v.toFixed(1),l-6,Y(v)+4);ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(i*3,X(i*3),bottom+17)}ctx.fillText('Time (s)',(l+r)/2,209);ctx.textAlign='left';ctx.fillText(unit,l,11);for(const s of series){ctx.strokeStyle=s.color;ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.setLineDash(s.key==='open'?[4,4]:[]);ctx.beginPath();c[s.key].data.forEach((row,i)=>{if(i)ctx.lineTo(X(row[0]),Y(row[s.col]*s.factor));else ctx.moveTo(X(row[0]),Y(row[s.col]*s.factor))});ctx.stroke()}ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.strokeStyle='#173443';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(t),top);ctx.lineTo(X(t),bottom);ctx.stroke()}
function playbackEnd(){return c.lqr.data[c.lqr.data.length-1][0]}
function draw(){if(!c)return;$('time').value=t;$('time-label').textContent=t.toFixed(!interactive&&t>=playbackEnd()&&c.lqr.metrics.status!=='completed'?3:2)+' s';rig('lqr');if(interactive)return;const plotFrame=Math.floor(t*12);if(plotFrame===lastPlot&&t<playbackEnd())return;lastPlot=plotFrame;const angles=[3,5,7].map((col,i)=>({key:'lqr',col,factor:180/Math.PI,color:[teal,purple,'#d78b32'][i]}));plot('angles',angles,'deg');plot('position',[{key:'lqr',col:1,factor:1,color:teal}],'m');plot('force',[{key:'lqr',col:9,factor:1,color:teal}],'N')}

function pause(){playing=false;cancelAnimationFrame(raf);$('play').textContent='Play'}
function choose(){pause();clearInteraction();t=0;c=D.cases[$('case').value];$('time').max=playbackEnd();$('time').step='any';scene=sceneBounds();lastPlot=-1;$('explanation').textContent={swingup:'All three links start hanging at 180°, with zero velocity. A six-second reference manoeuvre is followed by upright balancing.',aligned:'All three links start at +1° from vertical. Target: upright with the cart at x = 0 m.',opposed:'Failed recovery: initial angles +1°, −1°, +1°. The 8 N actuator saturates and the run reaches the angle cutoff. Local LQR stability does not guarantee recovery under saturation.',push:'The three links start exactly upright. The cart receives a 3 N push from 4.0 to 4.2 s.'}[$('case').value];$('control-title').textContent=$('case').value==='swingup'?'Planned swing-up + LQR':'Eight-state LQR';const m=c.lqr.metrics;$('metrics').innerHTML=`<tr><td>Triple · feedback</td><td>${m.status==='completed'?'Completed 12 s':m.status==='tilt_limit'?'Stopped: angle limit':'Stopped: travel limit'}</td><td>${m.settling_s===null?'Not settled':m.settling_s.toFixed(2)+' s'}</td><td>${m.peak_force_N.toFixed(2)} N</td><td>${m.effort_N2s.toFixed(2)} N²·s</td></tr>`;if($('case').value==='push')for(const v of D.push_comparison||[]){$('metrics').innerHTML+=`<tr><td>${v.name}</td><td>${v.status==='completed'?'Completed 12 s':v.status}</td><td>${v.settling_s===null?'Not settled':v.settling_s.toFixed(2)+' s'}</td><td>${v.peak_force_N.toFixed(2)} N</td><td>${v.effort_N2s.toFixed(2)} N²·s</td></tr>`}draw()}

function clearInteraction(){interactive=null;drag=null;dragId=null;liveTrail=[];accumulator=0;physicalStop=false;recovery=null;lastPlot=-1;$('recorded-plots').hidden=false;$('recorded-results').hidden=false;$('time').disabled=false;$('interaction-note').textContent='Grab any coloured joint. The dashed tether applies a physical force; all three free hinges and rigid links respond together. Only the cart is motorised. After release, recovery may first settle the links downward, then raise them again. This can take tens of seconds; watch the phase label.'}
function tick(now){if(!playing)return;const elapsed=Math.max(0,Math.min((now-last)/1000,.05))*(Number($('speed').value)||1);last=now;if(interactive){accumulator+=elapsed;while(accumulator>=.00125){if(drag){const f=1-Math.exp(-.00125/.05);drag.x+=(drag.targetX-drag.x)*f;drag.y+=(drag.targetY-drag.y)*f;drag.strength=Math.min(1,drag.strength+.00125/.08)}const next=recovery.step(interactive,drag,.00125);if(!next.every(Number.isFinite)){physicalStop=true;pause();break}interactive=next;t+=.00125;accumulator-=.00125;if(Math.abs(interactive[0])>2){physicalStop=true;pause();drag=null;dragId=null;break}}liveTrail.push([t,...interactive,0,0]);while(liveTrail.length>2&&liveTrail[1][0]<t-1.05)liveTrail.shift()}else t=Math.min(playbackEnd(),t+elapsed);draw();if(t>=playbackEnd()&&!interactive)pause();else if(playing)raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}
const grabCanvas=$('lqr');function pointerWorld(e){const r=grabCanvas.getBoundingClientRect();return{x:((e.clientX-r.left)*grabCanvas.clientWidth/r.width-view.ox)/view.scale,y:(view.oy-(e.clientY-r.top)*560/r.height)/view.scale}}
grabCanvas.onpointerdown=e=>{if(drag||physicalStop)return;const q=pointerWorld(e),row=interactive?[t,...interactive,0,0]:sample(c.lqr.data,t),p=joints(row);let point=0,best=26/view.scale;for(let i=1;i<=3;i++){const dist=Math.hypot(q.x-p[i][0],q.y-p[i][1]);if(dist<best){point=i;best=dist}}if(!point)return;e.preventDefault();if(!interactive){interactive=row.slice(1,9);recovery=new RecoveryControl(D,$('case').value,t);liveTrail=[[t,...interactive,0,0]]}drag={point,x:p[point][0],y:p[point][1],targetX:p[point][0],targetY:p[point][1],offsetX:q.x-p[point][0],offsetY:q.y-p[point][1],strength:0};dragId=e.pointerId;grabCanvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);$('recorded-plots').hidden=true;$('recorded-results').hidden=true;$('time').disabled=true;$('control-title').textContent='Live physics · cart-only control';$('interaction-note').textContent='LIVE PHYSICS: the mouse applies an external force to one mass; all hinges remain free. Only the cart is controlled. After a large disturbance, the controller first settles the links downward, then relaunches swing-up. No state is reset. Recovery can take tens of seconds and is not guaranteed for every perturbation. Recorded metrics are hidden because this is now a new trajectory. Restart replays the original trial.';if(!playing){playing=true;last=performance.now();$('play').textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}draw()};
grabCanvas.onpointermove=e=>{if(drag&&e.pointerId===dragId){const q=pointerWorld(e);drag.targetX=Math.max(scene.xmin+.05,Math.min(scene.xmax-.05,q.x-drag.offsetX));drag.targetY=Math.max(-.52,Math.min(.52,q.y-drag.offsetY));e.preventDefault()}};
function releasePoint(e){if(dragId!==null&&e.pointerId!==undefined&&e.pointerId!==dragId)return;drag=null;dragId=null;draw()}
grabCanvas.onpointerup=releasePoint;grabCanvas.onpointercancel=releasePoint;grabCanvas.onlostpointercapture=releasePoint;

$('play').onclick=()=>{if(physicalStop)return;if(playing)pause();else{if(t>=playbackEnd()&&!interactive){t=0;lastPlot=-1};playing=true;last=performance.now();$('play').textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}};$('reset').onclick=choose;$('case').onchange=choose;$('time').oninput=e=>{pause();clearInteraction();t=Math.max(0,Math.min(playbackEnd(),Number(e.target.value)));draw()};document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden){pause();drag=null;dragId=null;}});matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').addEventListener('change',pause);let timer;new ResizeObserver(()=>{clearTimeout(timer);timer=setTimeout(()=>{lastPlot=-1;draw()},80)}).observe(document.querySelector('main'));$('gain').textContent='K = ['+D.gain.map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(', ')+'] in the state order [x, v, θ₁, ω₁, θ₂, ω₂, θ₃, ω₃].';if(!D.cases.swingup){$('swing-option').disabled=true;$('case').value='aligned';$('planning-note').textContent='Swing-up is not published: no physically validated reference is available yet.'}choose();})();
</script><script>__LIVE_PHYSICS__</script><script>__RECOVERY_CONTROL__</script></body></html>